<p>Ukraine&#x27;s National Anti-Corruption Bureau and Specialized Anti-Corruption Prosecutor&#x27;s Office named Andriy Yermak, President Volodymyr Zelenskyy&#x27;s former chief of staff, as an official suspect in a money-laundering investigation involving 460 million hryvnias, about $10.5 million, tied to a luxury residential project near Kyiv. Yermak appeared in court in Kyiv on Tuesday for a preventive-measure hearing. Reports described the notice as one of the most prominent moves by Ukraine&#x27;s anti-corruption bodies against a former senior figure in Zelenskyy&#x27;s administration.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/3XUylfJgCO1_k_nf-TeOxJNxRDi40znI4JnkQb3OuKZzcahvaupj-H6HAu7Pezc21cg26SVYEyMHHuZQ1A2a2g5IW3eDPZ0b_IK2EYF-7nL2vofj6PZhXhpvIeF6p2VRZ9N1qMKYqtKwv61HQoCHASZ4EmonE-DGzFKcv1QaaVIpsu2pD6E-R3pj77whlGEhqPvAsPB3a6KFOK0_cQCKBnehfbD_q7nkdHDYOTct0dsGZ6jULS5j1I9PzK_ta616sxOAxFK-In5aozX6PQ' alt='Former Head of the Presidential Office Andriy Yermak, a suspect in a corruption probe, appears at court for a hearing in Kyiv on May 12, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Searches: Le Temps reported a search involving Yermak on Monday evening and said he would speak once investigators finished their work.</li><li>Former senior aide: Yermak was described as one of Ukraine&#x27;s most influential unelected officials and had served as Kyiv&#x27;s chief negotiator in U.S.-supported peace talks with Russia.</li><li>Ownership denial: Yermak told Radio Liberty he did not own property in the housing development and declined to comment further on the allegations.</li><li>Separate schedule: On the same day, Zelenskyy met Palantir Technologies CEO Alexander Karp in Kyiv to discuss cooperation with the U.S. defense sector.</li></ul><blockquote>The President of Ukraine has neither been nor is currently a subject of the investigation - Head of Ukraine&#x27;s National Anti-Corruption Bureau</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Andriy Yermak: Yermak said public pressure on law enforcement agencies drove allegations linking him to a group accused of laundering illicitly obtained funds. (<a href='https://english.nv.ua/nation/ex-presidential-office-head-yermak-says-corruption-suspicion-fueled-by-pressure-50607305.html'>NV</a>)</li><li>Ihor Fomin, Yermak&#x27;s lawyer: Fomin called the notice of suspicion groundless and said his client had no role in the real estate laundering allegations. (<a href='https://english.nv.ua/nation/yermak-lawyer-denies-role-in-kyiv-real-estate-case-50607278.html'>NV</a>)</li><li>Dmytro Lytvyn, Zelenskyy communications adviser: Lytvyn told reporters the president&#x27;s office would not comment substantively while procedural steps in the case continued. (<a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/zelenskiys-former-chief-of-staff-named-in-major-corruption-investigation-554237/'>Minute Mirror</a>)</li><li>NABU and SAPO: The agencies framed the allegation as participation in a criminal group accused of laundering illicit funds. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/12/zelenskyy-ex-chief-of-staff-andriy-yermak-accused-ukraine-corruption-investigation'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/zelenskyys-ex-chief-of-staff-a-suspect-in-a-money-laundering-probe-ukraine-officials-say'>Zelenskyy&#x27;s ex-chief of staff a suspect in a money-laundering probe, Ukraine officials say</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/13/zelenskyys-ex-chief-of-staff-appears-in-court-in-money-laundering-case'>Zelenskyy’s ex-chief of staff appears in court in money-laundering case</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-ukraine-zelensky-aide-suspect-money-laundering-probe/'>Zelensky’s former chief of staff named as suspect in major money-laundering probe</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/05/12/zelensky-s-former-chief-of-staff-denies-money-laundering-charges'>